emaining modalities, and the planner is informed of the reduced field of view and of the larger covariance (a larger protection level). A miscalibrated sensor shows a normal detection rate but a biased innovation whose sign is consistent and, for a temporal offset, grows with the relative velocity (Problem~\ref{prob:ch08:3}): the sensor is discounted, online calibration is triggered, and the planner receives a degraded-integrity flag with the inflated covariance. If either condition persists beyond a pre-defined time and the remaining sensors cannot meet the required integrity, the policy requests a minimal-risk manoeuvre.
